  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is being pulled by some men, up an inclined plane of inclination&nbsp;<math><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;and coefficient of friction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, as shown in the figure. If each man can apply a maximum force of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, then&nbsp;the minimum number of men required to just slide the block, up the plane is<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image5-844f2876-af25-4873-a127-75880623b1f4.jpg\" style=\"width: 251px; height: 172px;\" />",
